  "abstract": "<jats:p>We demonstrate an O-band Transmitter Optical Sub-Assembly (TOSA) based on thin-film lithium niobate (TFLN) technology for intensity-modulation direct-detection (IM-DD) applications at 400 Gb/s per lane and beyond. Through co-design of the TFLN modulator and a high-speed electronic driver, combined with optimized assembly techniques, the TOSA achieves 210 GBaud / 420 Gb/s PAM-4 operation with clearly open optical eye diagrams.</jats:p>",
